{"title":"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When simplified, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/8/a486f2bb9d92b450d88d0de2d3e4a1431b4352e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2 + \\frac{2}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"48\" height=\"45\" /> is equal to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/9/9a95532e5c0da4e613b7dac807eff527f2bd4351.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ \\frac{1}{8} \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ \\frac{5}{2} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ \\frac{5}{8} \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ \\frac{3}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"408\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we can get rid of the fraction in the denominator by multiplying the numerator and denominator of the fraction by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This gives:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/4/a644ea28b9bc53d6618636b0c1bf26377c4a93c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2 + \\frac{2}{3}} = \\frac{1 \\times 3}{(2 + \\frac{2}{3}) \\times 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"163\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/6/0f6c8964b28d4906f9b6837e8076b71c91cf59de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{3}{2 \\times 3 + \\frac{2}{3} \\times 3} = \\frac{3}{6 + 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"198\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/9/9898b275823dd38ded0afffe6b1d115fe32febd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\boxed {\\textbf {(E) } \\frac{3}{8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"79\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley\">2010 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2010 C